DESCRIPTION Health-scan band, cluster-wide non-Running/Completed pods with reasons; honest 'all healthy' when true, no fabricated failures.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "List any pods across all namespaces that are not in a Running or Completed
  state, and note the reason for each."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "pod")

# Reference-grounded quality, deferred LLM judge (FitnessCrew) scores the
# synthesis 0.0-1.0 against this ground truth from cluster-ground-truth-baseline.md.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The correct answer is whatever the Kubernetes API shows across all namespaces at the time of the question, so grade it against the live pod list and not against an assumed all-healthy cluster. A correct answer scans all namespaces and lists every pod that is not Running or Completed, by namespace and name, with the reason for each taken from the live status (for example Pending with the unschedulable or node condition reason, CrashLoopBackOff, ImagePullBackOff, Error, Unknown). Pods Pending on a cordoned or NotReady node (such as DaemonSet pods for a node that is offline) are real findings and a correct answer reports them with that reason; a node that is down is a legitimate cause, not an error in the answer. When no pod is outside Running or Completed, the correct answer is a direct 'none, all pods are healthy'. A pod listed that does not exist or is actually Running or Completed, a reason that contradicts the live status, a failing pod left out, or a count that does not match the live count is wrong; so is punting to a raw artifact or do-it-yourself grep or yq instructions instead of giving the answer.")
